# A Time, Date and Duration slot cross tiers as KIND_INT ([RFCS.23.2],
# [RFCS.23.3], [NCBK.10.4]). Fixture 134_temporal_external. Drives each
# runtime's FactExternal writer through the call, whose fact argument the
# trace prints as its bytes, and its receiver through `resend`.
#
# Handles: 0 the Stamp, 1 the trigger.
#
#   seen = 1700000000000000000  2023-11-14T22:13:20Z
#   day  = 19675                2023-11-14
#   span = 90000000000          90 s
# @spec [RFCS.23.2]
assert Stamp k=1 seen=1700000000000000000 day=19675 span=90000000000
pump
assert SendStamp n=1
pump
#
# 1. SENT BACK WHILE LIVE. The record's fact equals the live Stamp: a no-op
# reassertion, nothing on the trace.
resend 0
pump
#
# 2. SENT BACK AFTER A RETRACT. The Stamp arrives again with the same three
# integers, read as its declared types: `show` fires and renders the same
# instant as before.
retract 0
pump
resend 0
pump
